{"agent":"padapt2","data":{"budget":"","claim":"shutil.copytree(s, s/sub, dirs_exist_ok=True) returns (no exception) and copies one level deep into the subtree; FakeFs.copy_tree raises ValueError there, so the fake diverges from LocalFs.","falsifier":"shutil.copytree(s, s/sub, dirs_exist_ok=True) raises Error/ValueError (it does not)","item":"ADP-fs-fake-parity","mechanism":"shutil.copytree snapshots os.scandir(src) entries before os.makedirs(dst, exist_ok=True) and iterates the snapshot, so a dst inside src terminates after one level","probe":"scratch python3 shutil.copytree(s, s/sub, dirs_exist_ok=True) on a nested tree {s/top.txt, s/sub/deep/d.txt, s/sub/n.txt}","probe_output":"RETURNED OK; tree gains s/sub/top.txt and s/sub/sub/{deep/d.txt,n.txt}. move(file,file)/move(dir,dir) no-op OK. copytree(s,s,dirs_exist_ok=True)=shutil.Error; copytree(s,s/sub) dirs_exist_ok=False=FileExistsError.","question":"Does FakeFs.copy_tree diverge from shutil.copytree / LocalFs on copy-into-own-subtree with dirs_exist_ok=True, and must the fake raise ValueError there?","sources":[],"verdict":"CONFIRMED"},"id":"e4ca03c1b49b868a57b24c7f9","kind":"research.recorded","lamport":150332,"schema":1,"subject":"R0bb17d1207","ts":"2026-11-07T19:57:46.925105Z"}
